; Default exercise definitions
;
; An exercise is recorded within an activity and allows you to define the
; precise type and amount of work you did. Ex. bench_press, lap_400m, plank.
;
; An exercise has a name and 1 - 4 "slots" where you can record load, reps,
; duration, and/or distance.
;
; Definition syntax:
;   exercise <name> <slot> [slot...]
;
; [slot] can be one of `load`, `reps`, `duration`, `distance`
;
; `load` is measured in mass, which can be one of `lb`, `kg`
; `reps` is measured in count, which is unitless
; `duration` is measured in time, which is one of `sec`, `min`, `hr`
; `distance` is measured in distance, which is one of `m`, `km`, `mi`, `ft`, `yd`
;
; Record syntax:
;   2026-08-05 lift "My Lifting Activity"
;     <exercise_name> <exercise_slot_value...>
;
; When recording an exercise, values for all defined slots must be specified.
;
; Slash-listing may be used on up to one slot to repeat that exercise with the
; specified slot values. The other slot values are copied to each repeated
; record.
;
; Example of bench press with 185 lb of weight across 5 reps, 5 reps, 4 reps:
;   bench_press 185 lb 5/5/4
;
; Example of 400m lap with varying durations:
;   lap_400m 92/94/91 sec
;
; Commas can be used as a shorthand for definition repeated exercises with
; different values.
;
; Example of multiple farmer carrys:
;   farmer_carry 90 lb 40/40/35 m, 70 lb 45 m

